WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
The same five friends, the same rule.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.400
This time, every car has only two seats.

3
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.550
Friends ride together —

4
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.550
but does it fit?

5
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:22.610
The rule gains one line: before merging, check that it fits.

6
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:27.410
A candidate that does not fit is crossed out, however close.

7
00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:31.321
Among the rest, take the closest pair.

8
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.356
Ada and Ben take the first two-seater.

9
00:00:41.356 --> 00:00:47.933
Three with Cai won't fit; Dev and Eva take the second.

10
00:00:47.933 --> 00:00:50.956
Cai has to ride alone.

11
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.869
Is the rule too dumb? Count the seats.

12
00:00:54.869 --> 00:00:58.469
Five people, two seats a car.

13
00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:05.869
Five divided by two, rounded up: at least three. Two cars is impossible for anyone.

14
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:13.000
Three-seat taxis: Ada and Ben carry cellos, two seats each.

15
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.933
The two best friends ride first.

16
00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:19.178
Anyone more overflows: three taxis.

17
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.404
But Ada with Cai, Ben with Dev —

18
00:01:25.404 --> 00:01:28.404
two taxis, exactly full.

19
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.600
Stopping does not mean there is no answer.

20
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.867
Greedy grabbed the biggest bond and never went back.

21
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:47.522
Day two, tandem bikes: Ada and Ben share one.

22
00:01:47.522 --> 00:01:52.767
Cai and Dev take the other: two 9s split, 18 in all.

23
00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:56.767
Swap partners: only 11 is split.

24
00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:02.292
Three stories, three endings.

25
00:02:02.292 --> 00:02:05.892
Impossible: no one can do it.

26
00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:10.026
Stuck: an answer exists, and greedy missed it.

27
00:02:10.026 --> 00:02:13.937
Not the best: legal, but it could be better.

28
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:20.560
On a chip, each region holds only so much area; clusters must fit too.

29
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.500
Legal is not the same as done.

30
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:33.500
Done is not the same as best.

31
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:40.500
When it stops, say which one it is.

32
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:48.500
What if nodes don't merge, only change labels? See the next module.

33
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:56.600
In the lab below, change the capacity or a size and read the diagnosis.
